// A handle's type arguments are written as Avin writes boundary types: no type of Sysl's own, no
// `Option` or `Result` of the wrong number of arguments, no empty argument, and nothing after the
// closing bracket.
// error: `u32` cannot be a type argument of the Sysl type a handle is on: each is one Sysl type, an integer of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, `byte`, `real`, `char`, `bool`, `unit`, `string`, or an `Option`, a `Result` or a tuple of these
// error: `Option[int, long]` cannot be a type argument of the Sysl type a handle is on: each is one Sysl type, an integer of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, `byte`, `real`, `char`, `bool`, `unit`, `string`, or an `Option`, a `Result` or a tuple of these
// error: `Result[int]` cannot be a type argument of the Sysl type a handle is on: each is one Sysl type, an integer of 8, 16, 32 or 64 bits, `byte`, `real`, `char`, `bool`, `unit`, `string`, or an `Option`, a `Result` or a tuple of these
// error: `@sysl` on a class names the Sysl type it is a handle on, by its module and name, as in `sysl.checksum.Crc32`, or an instance of a generic one, as in `sysl.buf.Buf[int]`; `pkg.views.Pair[int, ]` is not one
// error: `@sysl` on a class names the Sysl type it is a handle on, by its module and name, as in `sysl.checksum.Crc32`, or an instance of a generic one, as in `sysl.buf.Buf[int]`; `pkg.views.Signal[int].x` is not one

@sysl("pkg.views.Signal[u32]")
class Unsigned

@sysl("pkg.views.Signal[Option[int, long]]")
class TwoOptions

@sysl("pkg.views.Signal[Result[int]]")
class OneResult

@sysl("pkg.views.Pair[int, ]")
class Missing

@sysl("pkg.views.Signal[int].x")
class Trailing

main() = ()
